146: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
147:     """
148:     Transfer sprites from red-tagged lanes into green-tagged lanes using a top-first destination fill, with all role markers moved to the top edge.
149: 
150:     Input structure:
151:     - The background is the most common color. Thin red (2) and green (3) 1x5 bars on row 0 identify source and destination lanes.
152:     - Each fixed lane contains repeated monochrome plus sprites on a regular vertical lattice, and the destination lane's visible sprites still occupy ordinary lane slots rather than touching the top-row marker.
153: 
154:     Rule:
155:     - Every sprite in a red-marked lane turns grey (5), while the same number of copies is inserted into the nearest green-marked lane using that lane's own color.
156:     - The destination lane fills its highest empty legal slots first, proceeding downward through the lattice instead of growing upward from the bottom cluster.
157:     - After all transfers, both red and green marker bars are erased back to the background.
158: 
159:     Key insight:
160:     - The top-row bars still reveal which lanes donate and receive, but the placement logic must be rebuilt from the destination lane's lattice: enumerate all legal slot rows and choose empty ones from top to bottom.
161:     """
