49: 2. Complexity calibration
50:    - If the generator allowed only one pair, reversing the right stack would be invisible.
51:    - If repeated colors were common, the reverse-pair swap could collapse into an output that looks
52:      identical to a simpler non-fused variant.
53:    - To keep the rule visible but still simple, the generator uses:
54:        * equal counts for frames and solids;
55:        * at least 2 pairs;
56:        * unique colors across all objects.
57:      This gives repeated structural evidence for both parts of the combo without introducing extra
58:      markers, hidden numeric ordering, or noisy object classes.
59: 
60: 3. Implicit-assumption audit of the original `main()`
61:    - `bg = get_bg(g)` still holds: the background remains the dominant color.
62:    - `find_components(... monochromatic=False)` still assumes each object is an isolated connected
